> Hi Mauro,
> Thanks for testing and for the report. This is vaguely reminiscent of
> some i386 assembler issue we fixed back in the kernel in the 5.9
> release.
> https://github.com/ClangBuiltLinux/linux/issues/194
> So definitely surprising to see something similar in mainline; perhaps
> config related, or something should be a feature check rather than a
> version check.
>
> To start with, do you mind sharing your .config file? If I can repro
> with ToT LLVM, then this may be an issue to fix given such a .config.

I have checked also with kernel-5.17 and the same build error is
happening also there,
so it is not due to commit 34737e2698 ("uaccess: add generic
__{get,put}_kernel_nofault")

In the attachments the defconfig files I am using to build ARCH=x86
kernel target

Here follows the kernel.mk script used in our Android 11 derived
project, which is similar to reference aosp kernel build script:
http://git.osdn.net/view?p=android-x86/device-generic-common.git;a=blob;f=build/tasks/kernel.mk;h=0bd2dc8f45854639e031402d3e3a738574878c67;hb=refs/heads/r-x86

Basically when building with BUILD_KERNEL_WITH_CLANG=true we're
issuing the following variable in make command:

CROSS_COMPILE := x86_64-linux-androidkernel-
HOSTCC=$(abspath $(LLVM_PREBUILTS_PATH)/clang)
CC=$(abspath $(LLVM_PREBUILTS_PATH)/clang)
CLANG_TRIPLE=x86_64-linux-gnu-

>
> Otherwise, I'll need to see what's different between upsteam llvm's
> release/11.x branch, and that release of AOSP clang.
>
> Orthogonally, I think the latest release of AOSP clang is 14.0.5. Any
> reason you're still using 11.0.2?  I expect to drop support for 11
> next.

I am using 11.0.2 because it is provided by aosp for Android 11,
but I am trying to build the x86 32bit kernel with android-12.1.0_r4
where prebuilt toolchain has clang version 12.0.7

I have also tried to checkout more recent clang and tamper with
Android build/soong/cc/config/global.go in a similar manner to [1] in
order to set the toolchain of an updated version, but the result is
not guaranteed to build, I often get dozens of building errors,
and that is to be expected because with newer clang version there are
a lot of changes (cflags, go script changes and sometimes code too).

To avoid showstoppers I usually stick to the clang toolchain shipped
by AOSP, as the kernel should build with those, considering that aosp
has x86 32bit kernel targets too.

So I will report on x86 32bit target build attempt with
android-12.1.0_r4 / clang version 12.0.7

As far as I remeber x86 32bit target has always been tricky, maybe I
am doing some gross mistake,
if this is the case I apologize in advance


[1] https://android.googlesource.com/platform/build/soong/+/e1d067b529545c308c2caa2fcbb29a6aacb7deb2%5E1..e1d067b529545c308c2caa2fcbb29a6aacb7deb2/

